// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 2 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P3): the same LOCAL text pushed twice into a
// GLOBAL list of text. Before the fix, a non-fresh push value disqualified
// only the value itself, never the receiving container -- `p3Gl`'s
// element-free loop (once globals were tracked at all, per Critical 1)
// would have freed `p3X`'s handle twice, once per element slot. The
// 4e/pre-ARC fix disqualified the receiver too, on the first non-fresh
// push: `p3Gl` never got an element-free loop, so both slots (aliasing the
// one handle) were simply abandoned. Expected 4e/pre-ARC leak count: 4 --
// `p3X`'s text (struct box + data handle, 2 blocks) plus `p3Gl`'s own list
// (struct box + backing-array handle, 2 blocks).
//
// ARC Task 5 (counted container element slots) closes this fixture to
// ZERO, by two independent, jointly-necessary changes, both confirmed
// against the emitted C:
//   1. EVERY push now retains its non-birth value first (`p3X` is a bare
//      identifier, non-birth) -- `p3Gl`'s TWO element slots each carry
//      their OWN +1 of the shared handle after both pushes run (rc==3:
//      `p3X`'s own original +1, plus one retain per push).
//   2. Task 5 DELETED the "non-fresh-push disqualifies the receiver"
//      consult that used to keep `p3Gl` out of ANY deep release --
//      `p3Gl` now qualifies for `cl_free_globals`'s real element-walk
//      release (`{ int32_t i; for (...) rt_text_release(*(rt_text
//      **)rt_list_at(cv_p3Gl, i)); } rt_list_release(cv_p3Gl);`), which
//      releases BOTH slots -- rc 3 -> 2 -> 1, still never zero from this
//      walk alone.
// `p3X` itself, as a LOCAL fed to two push arguments, is now a
// shallow-release-safe handoff (Task 5's own `lowEscapeWalkArgsSafeHandoff`
// -- the pushed-value argument no longer routes through `lowFreeUnsafe`'s
// full skip) -- confirmed against the emitted C: `rt_text_release(cv_p3X);`
// at scope exit, dropping rc 1 -> 0, the FINAL release that actually
// disposes the box. No leak, no double-free: the three releases (two
// element-walk, one local scope-exit) exactly balance the three owners
// (`p3X`'s own reference plus the two independent push retains).

var p3Gl: list of text

func runP3DupPush() {
    var p3X: text = "dup"
    p3Gl.push(p3X)
    p3Gl.push(p3X)
    alert("p3 done")
}
